---
const properties = [
  {
    name: 'Verifiable',
    verb: 'you can run it',
    definition:
      'A function returns the expected value or it doesn’t. A schema validates or it throws. A test suite is green or red. There is no "the vibes are slightly off."',
    detail:
      'Verification is what turns a probabilistic generator into something you can trust in production — and what the labs’ RLVR training loops optimize against.',
    example: 'assert check_playbook(contract) == []',
  },
  {
    name: 'Composable',
    verb: 'correctness stacks',
    definition:
      'Functions call functions, modules import modules. You build big correct things out of small correct things, and the correctness composes.',
    detail:
      'Prose doesn’t compose — you can’t import paragraph three into paragraph seven. Typed interfaces are what let a thousand small verifiers add up to one reliable system.',
    example: 'from playbook import check_liability_cap',
  },
  {
    name: 'Executable',
    verb: 'it is the action',
    definition:
      'Code isn’t a description of an action — it is the action. When an agent emits code, the environment changes and a feedback signal comes back.',
    detail:
      'Every step ends with ground truth: a file written, an API called, a number computed. That feedback is what agentic loops are made of.',
    example: 'result = run(candidate); errors = verify(result)',
  },
];
---

<section
  class="not-prose my-8 rounded-3xl border border-umai-gray-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-2xl shadow-umai-gray-900/10 dark:border-umai-gray-700 dark:bg-umai-gray-900/80 sm:p-6"
  aria-labelledby="code-substrate-title"
>
  <div class="mb-6 max-w-3xl border-b border-umai-gray-200 pb-5 dark:border-umai-gray-700">
    <div class="mb-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-umai-accent">why code wins</div>
    <h3 id="code-substrate-title" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-umai-primary dark:text-umai-secondary sm:text-3xl">
      Three properties of the code substrate
    </h3>
    <div class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-umai-gray-600 dark:text-umai-gray-300">
      Move a domain problem onto code and you inherit all three for free — and those three are
      exactly what turn a stateless next-token predictor into a reliable agent.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {properties.map((property) => (
      <article class="group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-umai-gray-200 bg-umai-gray-50 p-4 transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-umai-accent/50 hover:bg-white hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-umai-accent/10 dark:border-umai-gray-700 dark:bg-umai-gray-800/70 dark:hover:bg-umai-gray-800">
        <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-umai-accent to-umai-accent-light opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-300 group-hover:opacity-100"></div>
        <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <h4 class="font-mono text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-umai-gray-900 dark:text-white">{property.name}</h4>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-umai-accent/20 bg-umai-accent/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-umai-accent dark:border-umai-accent/30 dark:bg-umai-accent/15">
            {property.verb}
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-umai-gray-700 dark:text-umai-gray-200">{property.definition}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-umai-gray-500 dark:text-umai-gray-400">{property.detail}</p>
        <p class="mt-auto pt-4">
          <span class="block overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-umai-gray-900 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[0.7rem] text-green-400 dark:bg-umai-gray-900/90">
            {property.example}
          </span>
        </p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
